  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Emergency Assistance to Vulnerable People Affected by the Earthquake in Khoy, Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the 5.9 magnitude earthquake that occurred on 28 January 2023 in Khoy in north-western Iran, around 130,000 people are accommodated in 110 temporary sites managed by local authorities and the Iranian Red Crescent Society (IRCS) in 19 locations across Khoy Governorate. Based on an inter-agency multi-sectoral assessment conducted in the affected area highlighting a large spectrum of unmet needs presented by the affected population, in collaboration with local authorities, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is providing 4,900 individuals with USD 164,150 in unconditional multi-purpose cash assistance, allowing them to enhance access to adequate basic goods and supplies, and meet their basic needs in a secure and dignified manner. In collaboration with financial service providers, such as local banks, cash assistance will be provided through prepaid cards which will allow beneficiaries to either withdraw cash or execute payments for goods or services at points of sale.</narrative>
  </description>
